    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Spatial location and furniture",
     "texto": [
      "To say where a piece of furniture is, posture verbs such as «staan» (for things standing upright) or «liggen» (for flat things) are combined with spatial prepositions: «naast» (next to), «bij» (beside, near), «op» (on), «onder» (under). «Boven» means up or on the upper floor, and «beneden» means down."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
